# Review routing only. The branch ruleset on develop does not set
# require_code_owner_review, so nothing here blocks a merge — it decides who
# GitHub requests a review from.
#
# GitHub's softener for a required code-owner review is that an approval from
# any one of the owners is enough, which only helps when there is more than one.
# With a single owner who is also the usual author, requiring it would make
# every pull request unmergeable without a bypass, and a control that is
# bypassed is worse than an honest absence. Revisit if a second regular
# reviewer appears.
#
# Owners must have write permission; a read-only collaborator listed here is
# silently a no-op.

